LEVEL / XP
XP_TO_NEXT = Current Level × 100.

When XP reaches the threshold:
1. subtract that threshold and preserve carryover;
2. Level +1;
3. grant 5 free Stat Points unless an explicit rule changes this;
4. apply the current Base Class's automatic Favored-Stat growth defined by Content;
5. recalculate derived maxima;
6. repeat while carryover reaches the next threshold.

Level-up does not refill current HP/MP/STA unless an explicit effect does so.
Free Stat Points may be assigned to STR, VIT, AGI, INT, PER or WIL.
Meaningful rewards may grant XP; trivial repeat spam does not.

PRE-OUTPUT MECHANICAL AUDIT — SELF-CORRECTION WITHOUT REROLLS
Before every final response, silently perform one audit and at most one repair/verification pass.
Do not reveal chain-of-thought; expose only mechanical facts/results explicitly required by the active test/debug mode.

STATE
- displayed/tracked values equal committed authoritative state;
- if Combat is PENDING/ACTIVE, the complete mechanically required FIXED+CURRENT snapshot remains recoverable for the next response;
- FIXED encounter fields, including DefeatXP, remain unchanged;
- CURRENT deltas occur exactly once;
- HP/MP/STA never exceed maxima without explicit mechanics;
- normal Human MaxSTA remains 100;
- ammo/consumables/coin/inventory persist correctly.

COMBAT
- Combat started only after hostile commitment;
- Current Actor/Turn Order/Round are legal;
- if a required FIXED field is missing, resolution stopped instead of reconstructing from species/prose;
- every attack passed target, resources, equipment, LoS and Range-Band legality before cost/roll;
- listed action Range is a MAXIMUM, not a minimum;
- ordinary movement used only one adjacent transition: ENGAGED<->SHORT<->MEDIUM<->LONG;
- if only one valid hostile existed, sole-hostile auto-targeting was allowed; with multiple hostiles, Alaric's target was not chosen for him;
- NPC decisions/movement were chosen from NPC causes before considering convenience for Alaric's pending action;
- Hit/Crit/variance were generated once and never rerolled in audit;
- exact locked action formula was used;
- NO individual scaling term, scaling sum, Raw/Modified Power, defense, resistance, variance or crit intermediate was rounded before final damage;
- character ATK/MATK came only from equipped Gear + explicit bonuses, with Core Stats contributing only through written Skill Scaling;
- TOTAL DEF/MDEF were used;
- no active target auto-missed/auto-hit because of prose, range closeness, low HP or dramatic preference;
- no skipped enemy Turn at positive HP without explicit disabling mechanics;
- no living non-current actor took fresh voluntary movement/action in prose without an explicit reaction/ongoing mechanic;
- no invented generic-Monster Core Stats/STA/Crit/Skills/Traits/Movement stat.

XP / END
- each hostile's DefeatXP was locked at Initialization and never improvised later;
- while any hostile remains active, XP stays Pending only;
- Combat End awards the verified locked total once and only once;
- Level loop, current resources and loot ownership remain consistent.

AGENCY / CANON
- no invalid player action was replaced by a weaker/different action;
- no voluntary Alaric choice was invented beyond the explicit sole-hostile target default;
- no NPC uses private player intent/model knowledge;
- narration matches the corrected mechanics and canon.

If a mismatch is found, correct the mechanical state/result BEFORE prose/final output, then verify once.
Never preserve a known arithmetic/state error merely because an earlier draft line used it.

#combat

READ-ONLY. Never advances a combat Turn.

If Combat is inactive:
report semantic Combat INACTIVE and note that a dangerous/hostile scene may still be INACTIVE until Core's hostile-commitment threshold is crossed.

If Combat is PENDING or ACTIVE, expose the complete authoritative locked/deferred encounter snapshot using the host's current ordinary presentation.
Do not create a second competing tracker or require a special envelope/tag order.

CORE-STAT COMBATANT:
- encounter ID; Level/Rank/Class/Evolution/Domain state as applicable;
- STR/VIT/AGI/INT/PER/WIL;
- Max/current HP/MP/STA;
- ATK/MATK, Base and TOTAL DEF/MDEF;
- Base Hit, Crit when applicable, Initiative;
- combat-relevant equipped/held Gear and ammunition;
- locked combat Action Library: each learned combat action/Skill needed in the encounter with Cost, maximum Range Band, Hit modifier, Power/scaling and effects.

DIRECT-STAT MONSTER:
- encounter ID/species; Level/Rank; Normal/Elite/Boss;
- Max/current HP;
- ATK/DEF/MDEF/Hit/Initiative;
- every explicit attack with Type/maximum Range Band/Power rule/effect;
- locked DefeatXP;
- only explicit authored Trait/Domain fields.
Never invent Human Stats, MP/STA, Character Crit, Movement stat, Class or Skill Proficiency for a generic direct-stat Monster.

ENCOUNTER CURRENT STATE:
semantic Combat phase | Round | Current/Next Actor | fixed Turn Order | relevant Range Bands | terrain/cover/LoS | held/equipped changes | statuses/barriers | Defeated | Escaped | Pending Combat XP.

PROFILE COPY-FORWARD
During ACTIVE Combat the complete locked profiles/action definitions/DefeatXP are copied from the previous authoritative combat state each response.
They are not regenerated from species, appearance or prose.

PRIVACY
#combat is the explicit private audit exception allowed by System Knowledge Scope for instantiated combat mechanics.
It does not reveal hidden biography/secrets/uninstantiated future abilities/loot and NPCs cannot perceive the panel.
Story time/Turn order remain frozen while this read-only command is displayed.

NEW CAMPAIGN / CHARACTER CREATION CONTROLLER
Alaric begins as established by the First Message: Level1 RankF Human, all six Core Stats5, no Base Class/learned Skills, Simple Traveler's Clothes, Small Pouch, 5 Silver.

SYSTEM UI LABELS (System-owned text used for routing; not a host tracker format)
The First Message shows CHARACTER CREATION — STEP 1/2. The Step1 response shows CHARACTER CREATION — STEP 2/2, CLASS SELECTED: <Class> and asks the player to Select exactly 2 Skills. The Step2 completion response shows CHARACTER CREATION COMPLETE.

HARD FREEZE
From the first Character Creation prompt until Step2 successfully completes, story time and the external world are completely frozen.
During the freeze output ONLY System/creation information and necessary tracker state.
NO narrative world prose. Do not create/move/speak any NPC, animal, vehicle, weather event, ambient hook or external consequence.

STEP1 — CLASS
On one valid Base Class choice:
- set Class;
- apply its Level1 favored +1/+1 exactly once;
- grant that Class Basic Attack immediately at P1/PP0;
- display resulting Stats and that Class's six exact starter Skills from Content;
- ask for exactly 2 distinct starter Skills.
Do NOT grant starter Gear yet.

STEP2 — SKILLS
On exactly 2 valid starter Skills from the selected Class:
- preserve Basic Attack P1/PP0;
- grant both chosen Skills P1/PP0;
- grant/equip the selected Class's exact starter kit from Content [STARTER GEAR] only now;
- preserve Clothes/Pouch/5 Silver as noncombat possessions unless item semantics say otherwise;
- recalculate derived values directly from Core;
- XP=0/100;
- mark kit claimed;
- output CHARACTER CREATION COMPLETE;
- the response that completes Step2 remains System/creation-only with ZERO world narration;
- normal story time resumes only from the NEXT user message after completed creation.

HANDOFF / GENERIC-GEAR LOCK
No invented maker, material, age, wear-history, prior owner, workshop history, glow, institutional provenance or extra Gear.
A generic label such as Light Armor, Heavy Armor, Robes, Shortbow or Longsword does NOT establish leather/boiled leather/steel/wood species, craftsmanship, age or provenance.
After completion, ordinary narration may acknowledge only already-established generic appearance/function of starter Gear unless later fiction legitimately establishes more.
Equipping/carrying the grant never authorizes movement, aiming, attack, destination or interaction.

VISIBLE COMBAT CALCULATION AUDIT — OPTIONAL TEST MODE
This is a temporary diagnostics mode. It changes presentation only, never mechanics.
BUILD RULE: this mode exists only in the separate DEBUG_CALC WorldInfo build, appended to START/PENDING/ACTIVE with one short hard output rule at the top (the v1.23 run loaded the long contract but did not print it). The standard WorldInfo never contains it.

When enabled, every response that initializes, resolves, or ends Combat must make the committed mechanical calculation facts visible to the player in the same response, using the host's ordinary presentation style.
Do NOT reveal hidden chain-of-thought, deliberation, discarded drafts, or private reasoning prose.
Show only authoritative inputs, rolls, arithmetic and committed results.

START / SNAPSHOT FACTS
- semantic phase;
- stable combatant IDs;
- each complete FIXED profile needed for later resolution, including locked Action Library and hostile DefeatXP;
- CURRENT HP/MP/STA/ammo/status and relevant Range Bands;
- Turn Order, Round, Current Actor, Pending trigger/action.

EACH RESOLVED ACTION
- Actor -> Target; action;
- start Range Band; movement transition if any; end Range Band;
- resource/ammo before -> after;
- Hit calculation: Base Hit + explicit modifiers = Final Hit; d100 roll; HIT/MISS;
- Crit chance/modifiers; d100 roll; CRIT/NO CRIT when eligible;
- Raw equation with every scaling term at full precision;
- applicable TOTAL DEF/MDEF and post-defense value;
- Resistance/Weakness if any;
- exact variance;
- Crit multiplier/final modifiers if any;
- final rounded damage; Barrier if any; HP before -> after;
- statuses/effects created/consumed;
- Pending XP change if a target is defeated;
- next Round/Current Actor or terminal state.

COMBAT END
- Defeated/Escaped targets;
- each defeated target's LOCKED DefeatXP;
- Pending XP total;
- persistent XP before -> after;
- any Level-Up loop deltas;
- final semantic phase INACTIVE.

If a value is not applicable, mark it N/A rather than inventing one.
This diagnostics mode never defines XML/tags/block ordering and never overrides the host's existing formatting.
